From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:36:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] Cliffs data path: the validated cliffs.geojson loader,
 the rasteriser and the looks a map can give (pure, tested)

An optional per-site cliffs.geojson (lines or polygons with a bare-rock share, a rock style, a profile hint, credit and day) is read by a pure
validator that refuses a malformed file with plain sentences and never throws, and is put on the 10 m grid as three rasters. The style and
profile tables and the look code that rides in the rock mask's alpha are in render/cliffStyle.ts. Fixtures are synthetic and live under tests:
no cliff has been mapped and nothing is added to public/demo. Nothing reads any of it yet.

