From 5d7af75d2991e8494e076427ea1c34f3080e0921 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:36:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] Apply a hand-mapped cliffs map to the drawing only:
 rock share, style and profile

The map's rock share replaces the rock mask's R (the tree copy, scree and pavement follow it), its style and profile ride in the mask's alpha and
scale the rock detail in the terrain shader (one texel fetch, two small tables, no new sampler), and a profile scales how far the ground is
sharpened to be drawn. With no map every byte is what it was. The map goes from the loader to SceneView.setScenario and nowhere else; the
site's manifest decides whether the file is asked for, so no request is made and no code is loaded for a site without one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
